          "To insulate the sub-algebra A(Ω) against arbitrary local environmental operators Oi ∈B(HA), we embed the computational degrees of freedom into a topological quantum phase governed by a non-Abelian braided tensor category. Consider a (2 + 1)-dimensional topological quantum field theory described by an SU(2)k Chern-Simons gauge theory evaluated at Chern-Simons level k = 3, corresponding to the quan- tum deformation parameter: q = exp \u0012 iπ k + 2 \u0013 = exp \u0012iπ 5 \u0013 (6) The superselection sectors of this theory form the modular tensor category of Fibonacci anyons, denoted CFib.",
          "Theorem 2.1 (Fibonacci Anyon Algebraic Structure). The category CFib possesses exactly two simple isomorphism classes of objects: the trivial vacuum sector 1 and the non-Abelian anyon sector τ. They obey the single non-trivial fusion algebra: τ ⊗τ = 1 ⊕τ, 1 ⊗τ = τ ⊗1 = τ, 1 ⊗1 = 1 (7) The quantum dimensions da are the unique positive Frobenius-Perron eigenvalues of the fusion ma- trices Na: d1 = 1, dτ = φ = 1 + √ 5 2 ≈1.6180339887 (8) where φ2 = φ + 1 is the canonical golden ratio. 2",
          "Proposition 2.2 (Total Quantum Dimension and Universal Entanglement Offset). The total quan- tum dimension D of the category CFib evaluates to: D = s X a∈{1,τ} d2a = p 12 + φ2 = p 2 + φ = s 5 + √ 5 2 ≈1.9021130326 (9) For a smooth, contractible spatial disk Ω⊂Σ of perimeter boundary length L, the von Neumann entanglement entropy exhibits the universal Kitaev-Preskill / Levin-Wen expansion: S(Ω) = −Tr(ρA ln ρA) = αL −γ (10) where α is a non-universal UV boundary coefficient and the topological entanglement entropy is: γ = ln D = ln \u0010p 2 + φ \u0011 = 1 2 ln(2 + φ) ≈0.6429653775 (11)",
          "Proof. Let HE be the modular entanglement Hamiltonian defined by ρA = e−HE. By the replica trick, the n-th Rényi entropy evaluates as: Sn(Ω) = 1 1 −n ln Tr(ρn A) = 1 1 −n ln \u0012 Zn (Z1)n \u0013 (12) where Zn is the Euclidean partition function evaluated on an n-fold branched Riemann cover Σn branched over Ω. In a topological quantum field theory with boundary S1, surgery on the 3-manifold maps Zn to the modular S-matrix element S0 0 = D−1. Evaluating the asymptotic partition function: ln Zn = nαL −(n −1) ln D + O(L−1) (13) Taking the analytical continuation n →1 yields: S(Ω) = lim n→1 Sn(Ω) = αL −ln D (14) Because D = √2 + φ, we obtain γ = ln √2 + φ > 0.",
